&HEAD VERSION = 7700, TITLE = 'Blower door leakage check' /
!! Audit A01 (secondary defect) - the ceiling leak created from FLOW_COEFFICIENT has zero area (initialization.f90:284).
!! Closed 5 x 5 x 3 m room at ambient, FLOW_COEFFICIENT = 0.01 m3/(s Pa^0.5), exhaust fan of 0.05 m3/s.
!! Expected at steady state: fan flow = C * dP**0.5, so dP = (0.05/0.01)**2 = 25 Pa and PRS_1 = -25 Pa.
!! Observed on master: PRS_1 = -42.24 Pa (wall and floor leaks only, 85/110 = 77 % of the area).
!! With the ceiling leak fix: PRS_1 = -25.23 Pa.
&TIME SIMULATION = 300 PRINT = 100 SMOKEVIEW = 10 SPREADSHEET = 10 /
&INIT PRESSURE = 101325 RELATIVE_HUMIDITY = 50 INTERIOR_TEMPERATURE = 20 EXTERIOR_TEMPERATURE = 20 /
&COMP ID = 'Room' DEPTH = 5 HEIGHT = 3 WIDTH = 5 CEILING_MATL_ID = 'OFF' WALL_MATL_ID = 'OFF' FLOOR_MATL_ID = 'OFF' ORIGIN = 0, 0, 0 FLOW_COEFFICIENT = 0.01 /
&VENT TYPE = 'MECHANICAL' ID = 'Exhaust' COMP_IDS = 'Room', 'OUTSIDE' AREAS = 0.5, 0.5 HEIGHTS = 1.5, 1.5 FLOW = 0.05 CUTOFFS = 200, 300 OFFSETS = 1, 1 /
&TAIL /
